    <item>
      <title>Continuing Campus-Wide Walking Challenge &amp; Monday Walking Group at Blackburn Center (Armour J. Blackburn University Center)</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/53870566494903/huge/318b48f129d0785a6066c1bfe7ca0449e5c0d0f3.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Mon, 14 Sep 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>Walking lowers the risk of heart disease, helps manage weight, and strengthens muscles. It also reduces stress, clears the mind, and improves daily mood. All staff and faculty are invited to join in a campus-wide walking challenge that started August 24 and goes until October 2. Participants can still enroll, set goals, and track daily steps. Each week, two $50 gift cards will be given out to participants who meet the daily step requirements; at the end of the challenge three $100 gift cards will be awarded. Registration required. </p>

<p> </p>

<p>To support the challenge, an in-person walking group will meet every Monday (except Labor Day) in front of Blackburn Center.  Led by Howard University Wellness Champion, Alisha McDougal, and supported by the HR Wellness and Benefits team, participants will gather and walk together in a shady area around campus. This in-person group walk will be repeated every Monday during the challenge. Please bring your walking shoes and water.   </p>

<p> </p>

<p>For more information, contact Alisha McDougal at <a href="mailto:Alisha.McDougal@Howard.edu">Alisha.McDougal@Howard.edu</a> or Onsite Health Coach, Katherine Smith, at <a href="mailto:Katherine.Smith@Evernorth.com">Katherine.Smith@Evernorth.com</a>.</p>

<p><a href="https://events.howard.edu/event/continuingcampus-wide-walking-challengemonday-walking-group">View on site</a> | <a href="mailto:?subject=I found an interesting event%3A Continuing%C2%A0Campus-Wide Walking Challenge%C2%A0%26%C2%A0Monday Walking Group&amp;body=I found an interesting event you may like%3A%0A%0A%0ADate%3A Sep 14%2C 2026%0A%0ADescription%3A%0AWalking lowers the risk of heart disease%2C helps manage weight%2C and strengthens muscles. It also reduces stress%2C clears the mind%2C and improves daily mood. All staff and faculty are invited to join in a campus-wide walking challenge that started August 24 and goes until October 2. Participants can still enroll%2C set goals%2C and track daily steps. Each week%2C two %2450 gift cards will be given out to participants who meet the daily step requirements%3B at the end of the challenge three %24100 gift cards will be awarded. Registration required. %0A%0A %0A%0ATo support the challenge%2C an in-person walking group will meet every Monday %28except Labor Day%29 in front of Blackburn Center.  Led by Howard University Wellness Champion%2C Alisha McDougal%2C and supported by the HR Wellness and Benefits team%2C participants will gather and walk together in a shady area around campus. This in-person group walk will be repeated every Monday during the challenge. Please bring your walking shoes and water.   %0A%0A %0A%0AFor more information%2C contact Alisha McDougal at Alisha.McDougal%40Howard.edu or Onsite Health Coach%2C Katherine Smith%2C at Katherine.Smith%40Evernorth.com.%0A%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fevents.howard.edu%2Fevent%2Fcontinuingcampus-wide-walking-challengemonday-walking-group%0A">Email this event</a></p></div></div>]]></description>
